# Build context exclusions. Shrinks what Docker uploads to the daemon
# and prevents local artifacts from accidentally entering image layers.
#
# Anything not listed here is fair game for `COPY` in the Dockerfile.
# The Dockerfile only copies `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, and `src/`, so
# this list is conservative — its job is to avoid uploading useless
# bytes, not to enforce what's copied.

# Cargo build output — recreated inside the image, multi-GB locally.
target/

# Git history — never needed at build time; expensive to ship.
.git/
.gitignore

# CI/CD workflows — consumed by GitHub, not by the build.
.github/

# Documentation — large (~60KB combined) and irrelevant to the binary.
README.md
README_zh.md
LICENSE

# The Dockerfile / Makefile themselves.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
Makefile

# Editor / OS junk that might linger in the working tree.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
